@startuml
title How a session change updates a screen
hide footbox
skinparam backgroundColor #F8FAFC
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #DBEAFE
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #93C5FD
skinparam ArrowColor #475569
participant "Screen" as Screen
participant "useSession / React" as Hook
participant "Session store" as Store
participant "Auth controller" as Auth
Screen -> Hook : useSession()
Hook -> Store : subscribe(listener)
Store --> Hook : unsubscribe function
Hook -> Store : getSnapshot()
Store --> Hook : Current status, user and error
Hook --> Screen : Session data + actions
... User signs in successfully ...
Auth -> Store : commit(token, user, expectedVersion)
Store -> Store : Check version; save token\npublish authenticated snapshot
Store -> Hook : Call registered listener
Hook -> Store : getSnapshot()
Store --> Hook : New snapshot
Hook --> Screen : Render with updated session
... Component no longer needs subscription ...
Hook -> Store : unsubscribe()
note over Screen,Store
Provider supplies the session object.
The hook subscribes; tokens are not in the snapshot.
end note
@enduml
